131 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 118 0 R
/T (The proposed changes were developed by district leaders and district planning staff, guided by a set of criteria that reflect what the district is trying to achieve: schools large enough to offer stable, adequately resourced programming, buildings used well, and school communities kept together through change as much as possible.)
/E (The proposed changes were developed by district leaders and district planning staff, guided by a set of criteria that reflect what the district is trying to achieve: schools large enough to offer stable, adequately resourced programming, buildings used well, and school communities kept together through change as much as possible.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
132 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 118 0 R
/T (These criteria often pull in different directions. Keeping a school community together may require a larger boundary change. Consolidating a small immersion program may lengthen some students' trips. For that reason, the criteria were weighed against one another rather than applied as a fixed ranking, and the balance struck differs from one part of the city to another, because conditions differ.)
/E (These criteria often pull in different directions. Keeping a school community together may require a larger boundary change. Consolidating a small immersion program may lengthen some students' trips. For that reason, the criteria were weighed against one another rather than applied as a fixed ranking, and the balance struck differs from one part of the city to another, because conditions differ.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
133 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H5
/P 118 0 R
/T (Two scenarios were developed, which differ mainly in how many schools they close. A scenario that closes fewer schools affects fewer families and changes fewer boundaries, but leaves more schools below the enrollment at which a school can offer stable, fully resourced programming. A scenario that closes more schools does the reverse.)
/E (Two scenarios were developed, which differ mainly in how many schools they close. A scenario that closes fewer schools affects fewer families and changes fewer boundaries, but leaves more schools below the enrollment at which a school can offer stable, fully resourced programming. A scenario that closes more schools does the reverse.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [9]
>>
