596 0 obj
<<
/Title (The data and modeling team included all schools and programs across the district. As changes were modeled they were considered by region. Each region was formed based on two adjacent high school attendance areas. The four regions include Ida B. Wells and Lincoln on the west side, Jefferson and Roosevelt in the north, Grant and MacDaniel in the northeast, and Cleveland and Franklin in the southeast. The primary drivers of scenario development were to stabilize elementaries and middle schools, establish clear dual language immersion pathways, and reduce the number of split feeder patterns. Each of those schools was then compared with other schools in the same region using the criteria above. The result is a set of recommendations shaped not only by how a school's current enrollment compares to its sustainable threshold, but by the full set of priorities the district committed to weighing.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 306 0 R
/Next 650 0 R
>>
endobj
